    "short_description": "The Egyptian Customs Authority (ECA) is a governmental agency under the Ministry of Finance, established in 1947. It is headquartered primarily in Alexandria, with significant operations in Cairo. The ECA is responsible for regulating customs operations in Egypt, overseeing the clearance, inspection, and valuation of goods at ports, airports, and land borders.\n\nThe ECA provides essential customs services, including customs declarations, permit issuance for imports and exports, and enforcement of trade regulations. It manages the Arrival Notice Identification (ACID) system for shipment identification and handles complaints through dedicated hotlines and digital platforms. The authority serves a wide range of stakeholders, including importers, exporters, logistics companies, and government entities, ensuring compliance with customs laws and facilitating trade. A major restructuring plan is underway to modernize the ECA, with full implementation expected by late 2023.",
